I wrote the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md and committed it twice: a draft first, then the version with research findings. The build was already verified green by the harness. In this session I only ran the binary and one targeted test (the price-drift alarm), not the full suite.

The planner should look at these first:

1. **`/cost overcharges the model this loop runs on.** anthropic_preset (src/agent_builder.rs:758) matches model names by prefix, oldest first. So claude-opus-5-5, claude-fable-5-1 and claude-sonnet-5-5` get their older siblings' presets, and with them the older prices.
   • `yoyo model info claude-opus-5-5` prints $5/$25. The vendor's pricing page, fetched today, says $4/$20 with $0.20 cache hits. That overstates every Opus 5.5 session by 1.25x on input/output and 2.5x on cache reads.
   • Sonnet 5.5 cache hits are overstated 2x, and Fable 5.1 cache hits 4x.
   • Context window and output limits are the same in each pair, so cost is the only thing wrong.
   • yoagent 0.24.2 already has correct claude_opus_5_5() and claude_fable_5_1() presets. Sonnet 5.5 has none, so it needs its own entry with the vendor's rates, like Haiku 5.5 got.

2. **The price-drift alarm can't see these rows.** Running it lists `claude-opus-5-5`, `claude-sonnet-5-5`, `claude-fable-5-1` and `claude-haiku-5-5` as "rows yoyo cannot price". That's false: yoyo prices all four, three of them wrongly. The alarm checks a hand-written list of known model names instead of the rule the rest of yoyo uses, whose own comment says every surface should consult it. The same run still reports the 9 drifted non-Anthropic prices from the v0.2.0 release check. I haven't checked those against vendor pages.

3. **yoagent 0.25.0 came out today. Upgrading needs code changes and decisions, not just a version bump.**
   • Pricing is now off unless the app opts in with enable_bundled(). Without that call, /cost would quietly lose every yoagent preset price.
   • `AgentMessage::Extension was renamed to AgentMessage::Custom`, which breaks 5 places in yoyo. The compiler will flag these.
   • 0.24.3 moves "Overloaded" errors onto a retry path that ignores the retry_after_partial opt-in. That would bring back the evolve-loop failure from #997.
   • The upgrade also fixes two cancel bugs relevant to #988: tool calls that hadn't started could still run after Ctrl-C, and a cancelled sub-agent reported success.

4. **/model info anthropic/claude-opus-5 says 200k instead of 1M.** /cost already strips the anthropic/ prefix with strip_router_prefix, but model_context_window doesn't. The fix is to reuse that function.

5. **Leftovers from earlier work:** skill folders still haven't been checked against `--deny-dir` (#1002). The full size of the "prints failure, exits 0" problem (#982) is unknown until each command is tested.

Research: the Claude Code release notes added more cases of "a repo's own config can't loosen a setting" and "a symlinked settings file triggers a warning", plus HTTP hooks that block the action when they fail. I haven't checked what yoyo's hooks do on a timeout. Sonnet 5.5 shipped with breaking API changes. yoyo never sets tool_choice, so the forced-tool-use change doesn't hit it; I didn't probe the change to how thinking is turned off. I saved the measured prices and the yoagent 0.25 notes to yopedia.
